<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jorge Eliécer Gaitán</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1903">1903</a>–<a href="/years/1948">1948</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jorge Eliécer Gaitán was a Colombian lawyer and populist leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liberal-party-uk">Liberal Party</a>, mayor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bogota">Bogotá</a> in 1936 and the favourite for the next presidential election. His assassination in Bogotá on 9 April 1948 set off the riots of the Bogotazo, which destroyed much of the city centre. The killing deepened the conflict between Liberals and Conservatives known as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/la-violencia">La Violencia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jorge-eliecer-gaitan.jpg" alt="Jorge Eliécer Gaitán" width="320" height="404" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Revista Credencial Historia · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jorge_Eli%C3%A9cer_Gait%C3%A1n_(1936).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
